# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for known FALSE POSITIVES in libstdc++.
#
# When a task throws, the exception object is shared (ref-counted) between the
# worker thread's future state and the thread that calls future::get(). The
# refcount hand-off happens inside libstdc++.so, which is not compiled with
# TSan, so TSan cannot see the release/acquire ordering and reports a race
# between the reader of e.what() and whichever thread frees the object last.
# Reproduced WITHOUT this project: plain std::packaged_task + std::thread.
#
# Narrow on purpose: only destruction of a future's stored result.
race:std::__future_base::_Result*::~_Result